Medium:[ Linux in 2026: Why Millions Are Switching Away from Windows for Good](https://medium.com/@techinfintrix/linux-in-2026-why-millions-are-switching-away-from-windows-for-good-de104855bcdb)

[](https://medium.com/@techinfintrix?source=---byline--de104855bcdb---------------------------------------)

> Something unusual is happening on the world’s computers. Quietly, without a headline launch event or a billion-dollar marketing campaign, millions of ordinary users are walking away from Windows. Not because they have to. Not because someone told them to. But because, after years of patience wearing thin, they have finally had enough — and Linux has finally become good enough.

The article explains that past objections to the usage of Linux, such as difficulty of use or the lack of programs and games, are increasingly no longer an issue.&#x20;

In mid July 2026, the market share for Linux displayed by Statcounter was 7.56%:&#x20;

